<headroom-library version="1" id="clean-jangle-twelve" category="Clean" order="140" instrument="guitar" style="Indie / Jangle">
  <description>Ringing folk-rock and indie jangle: two compressors in series for long sustain, a bright clean blackface twin, a micro-pitch doubler that adds the shimmer of paired 12-string courses, and a short plate. Arpeggiate open chords high on the neck and let them ring.</description>
  <tags><tag>Clean</tag><tag>Indie / Jangle</tag><tag>Folk Rock</tag><tag>Compressed</tag><tag>Chime</tag></tags>
  <sources>
    <source url="https://www.vintageguitar.com/91957/jangle-of-the-rickenbacker-12/" title="Vintage Guitar: jangle of the Rickenbacker 12 (two tube compressors on McGuinn's direct signal)"/>
    <source url="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roger_McGuinn" title="Roger McGuinn (Wikipedia)"/>
    <source url="https://reverb.com/de/news/whats-that-sound-how-famous-moments-in-recording-history-were-made" title="Reverb: What's that sound? (McGuinn's conflicting accounts)"/>
    <source url="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/This_Charming_Man" title="This Charming Man (Wikipedia)"/>
    <source url="https://faroutmagazine.co.uk/the-guitar-secret-sound-the-smiths-johnny-marr/" title="Far Out: the guitar that was the sound of Johnny Marr"/>
  </sources>
</headroom-library>
</headroom-preset>
